                                                                                                                                                                                            <div class="ielts-standalone-q" data-qnum="33"><div class="ielts-q-header"><strong class="ielts-q-badge">33</strong><span class="ielts-q-title">The assumption today that people in the past knew very little about geography is correct.</span></div><div class="ielts-radio-group"><label class="ielts-radio-btn"><input type="radio" data-qnum="33" name="question_33" value="YES"><span class="ielts-radio-text"><strong>YES</strong> </span></label><label class="ielts-radio-btn"><input type="radio" data-qnum="33" name="question_33" value="NO"><span class="ielts-radio-text"><strong>NO</strong> </span></label><label class="ielts-radio-btn"><input type="radio" data-qnum="33" name="question_33" value="NOT GIVEN"><span class="ielts-radio-text"><strong>NOT GIVEN</strong> </span></label></div></div><div class="ielts-standalone-q" data-qnum="34"><div class="ielts-q-header"><strong class="ielts-q-badge">34</strong><span class="ielts-q-title">Plato was criticised for saying the world was shaped like a leather ball.</span></div><div class="ielts-radio-group"><label class="ielts-radio-btn"><input type="radio" data-qnum="34" name="question_34" value="YES"><span class="ielts-radio-text"><strong>YES</strong> </span></label><label class="ielts-radio-btn"><input type="radio" data-qnum="34" name="question_34" value="NO"><span class="ielts-radio-text"><strong>NO</strong> </span></label><label class="ielts-radio-btn"><input type="radio" data-qnum="34" name="question_34" value="NOT GIVEN"><span class="ielts-radio-text"><strong>NOT GIVEN</strong> </span></label></div></div><div class="ielts-standalone-q" data-qnum="35"><div class="ielts-q-header"><strong class="ielts-q-badge">35</strong><span class="ielts-q-title">The globe made by Crates of Mallus was an accurate representation of the known world.</span></div><div